# PSR-7d — Platform-ops identity design

## Intent

Design the replacement for the **shared static** `PLATFORM_OPS_BEARER_TOKEN`
(SoT PSR-7 item 1 / R-OPS-ID) **without changing `apps/api` in this wave**.

Doc-first covenant: any later code change to `assertPlatformOpsAuth` /
`read-platform-ops-bearer-token` must land only after this design is accepted.

## Current model (as-built)

```text
Client/BFF
  Authorization: Bearer <shared PLATFORM_OPS_BEARER_TOKEN>
  X-Platform-Ops-Phone: <E.164>
       │
       ▼
assertPlatformOpsAuth
  1) bearer === env shared secret (constant-time equality today: string ===)
  2) resolvePlatformOpsPhoneAccess(phone) → role owner|admin|support
       │
       ▼
PlatformAuthContext { actorId: phone, roles: [role] }
```

Parallel machine path (already closer to target):

- `verify-ops-service-jwt.ts` — short-lived JWT with **scopes**
  (`cache:invalidate`, `metrics:read`, `finance:recon`, `portal:entitlements`)
- `signPlatformOpsSessionToken` — RS256 JWT `kind: platform_ops`, **TTL 7d**,
  claims `platform_role` + `sub=phone` (session-ish; not yet the sole gate)

Gaps vs SoT:

| Requirement | Today |
| --- | --- |
| Short-lived | Shared bearer: **no**; session JWT: 7d (long); service JWT: yes |
| Scoped | Shared bearer: **no** (all-or-nothing + role); service JWT: **yes** |
| Rotatable without outage | Shared bearer: single env flip; JWT: key pair + previous-key slot on service path |
| Actor + audit | Phone as actorId; role from DB/env whitelist |

## Target model

```text
Human ops (Control Center BFF)
  Authorization: Bearer <platform_ops session JWT>
  — short TTL (≤15m access) + refresh or re-login
  — claims: kind=platform_ops, sub=phone, platform_role, scope[] (optional)
  — signed with AUTH_JWT_* key material; previous-key verify during rotation

Machine ops (internal routes)
  Authorization: Bearer <ops service JWT>
  — existing verifyOpsServiceJwt + scope enum (extend, do not fork)

Shared PLATFORM_OPS_BEARER_TOKEN
  — removed from production/prodlike after dual-accept window
  — test/dev may keep explicit fixture secret behind NODE_ENV=test only
```

### Auth decision tree (target)

1. Parse Bearer.
2. If JWT (three segments): verify as `platform_ops` session **or** ops-service
   (by `kind` / audience / scope claim). Reject shared-secret equality.
3. If opaque string: **deny** in production/prodlike; allow only in `NODE_ENV=test`
   with documented fixture.
4. Emit `PlatformAuthContext` with `actorId`, `roles`, and `scopes[]` for audit.

### Scope catalog (initial)

Reuse service scopes where possible; add human scopes only when a route needs
finer control than role:

| Scope | Who | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| (role-only) | human | Default: owner/admin/support gate as today |
| `finance:recon` | machine (+ maybe owner) | Existing |
| `cache:invalidate` | machine | Existing |
| `metrics:read` | machine | Existing |
| `portal:entitlements` | machine | Existing |

### Rollout slices (future; not this wave)

| Slice | Change | Risk |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **7d1** | Dual-accept: JWT session **or** shared bearer in `assertPlatformOpsAuth` | Low |
| **7d2** | BFF issues/refreshes short-TTL session JWT; stop sending shared bearer | Medium |
| **7d3** | Prodlike reject shared bearer; metrics for residual use | Medium |
| **7d4** | Delete shared-bearer reader path from prod codepaths; keep test fixture | Low |

## Non-goals (this wave)

- No edits under `apps/api/src/platform/**`
- No Control Center BFF wire
- No TTL change to existing `signPlatformOpsSessionToken` (7d → 15m is **7d1+**)
- No claim that R-OPS-ID is closed

## Smoke

```bash
node scripts/ops/psr-7d-ops-identity-design-smoke.mjs
```

## Next

Implement **PSR-7d1-dual-accept-session-jwt** only after Architect accepts this
design (and docs-first note before touching API). Alternate: live YES packs
(`PSR-6c6`, `R-BRANCH`, `R-STAGING`).
